+# HARNESS_LOG
+
+## Plan
+- Report: coaching reply "could not read" when reply is long / multi-line.
+- Suspect: `lib/claude-json.ts` `prepareJsonString` escapes ALL bare `\n`/`\t` (line 36), including
+  structural whitespace between JSON tokens. Pretty-printed JSON then becomes `{\n  "a"...` with a
+  literal backslash-n outside any string -> JSON.parse fails. Single-line replies happen to work, hence "sometimes".
+- Fix: replace the blanket regex with a small string-aware scanner that escapes raw `\n`, `\r`, `\t`
+  only while inside a JSON string literal (tracking `\` escapes), leaving structural whitespace alone.
+- Keep `lastIndexOf("}")` behaviour (existing KNOWN LIMITATION test asserts it; out of scope).
+- Verify with `npx vitest run lib/claude-json.test.ts`, then full `npx vitest run` and `npx tsc --noEmit`.
+
+## Log
+- Baseline (before edit): `npx vitest run` -> exit 1. Test Files 1 failed | 36 passed; Tests 4 failed | 276 passed.
+  All 4 failures in lib/claude-json.test.ts (pretty-printed JSON, newline in pretty JSON, escaped quote,
+  tab/CR in string). Error: "Expected property name or '}' in JSON at position 1" — confirms hypothesis.
+  (Running the single file `npx vitest run lib/claude-json.test.ts` was blocked by the permission prompt, so full suite was used.)
+- Change: lib/claude-json.ts — replaced blanket `\n`/`\t` regex with `escapeControlCharsInStrings`
+  (string-aware scanner; escapes raw \n, \r, \t only inside string literals).
+- After edit: `npx vitest run` -> Test Files 37 passed (37); Tests 280 passed (280).
+- After edit: `npx tsc --noEmit` -> exit 0, no output.
+- Callers checked via grep: app/api/coach/reflect/route.ts (extractJsonObject), app/api/dasha/route.ts (prepareJsonString).
